  "title": "🚶‍♂️ Brandenburg Walk Tour",
  "date": "2025-11-09T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "🚶‍♂️ Brandenburg Walk Tour\n\nBrandenburg is a quiet, conservative city about 70 km from Berlin. Compared to Berlin’s fast-paced, international vibe, locals here live closer to nature and prefer a slower rhythm of life. However, tourism isn’t a major focus — most people here don’t speak English, which makes the city feel more authentically local.\n\n🏨 Hotel\n\nThere aren’t many hotels in the city. The one I stayed in is just across the street from the university campus. It offers a student discount — €55 per night, including breakfast. 🥐☕\n\nHotel\n\n🎓 Campus\n\nThe Technische Hochschule Brandenburg (THB) campus is larger than Tallinn University’s.\n\nTechnischen Hochschule Brandenburg\n\nI also found the English translation on the toilet sign quite amusing — somehow polite and impolite at the same time. 😅\n\ntoilets notification\n\nHere’s the meal from the school canteen — €6.5, cash only. 💶\nThe food is decent, very typical of German campus meals.\n\nfood\n\nChicken Schnizel\n\nThai food\n\n🏰 Old Town\n\nBrandenburg has two historical centers:\n\nThe Old Town, built around the 15th century\n\nThe New Town, from the 17th century\n\nThe city wall has long been torn down, leaving only the gate tower standing as a reminder of the past.\n\nGate tower\n\nThe Old Town is full of beautiful brick architecture, giving the whole area a warm, timeless feel.\n\nCathelic\n\n🌉 New Town\n\nCross the lake and you’ll find yourself in the New Town — more modern, yet still peaceful and charming.\n\ncinema\n\nThe lake view is absolutely stunning — it feels like stepping into a painting. 🎨🌅\n\nlake view\nlake view\nlake view\n\n🍔 Food & Drinks\n\nIn the evening, we went to the Heartbeat Bar for burgers. It was my first time seeing schnitzel — a fried pork cutlet that’s super crispy and delicious.\n\nbeef burger\nSchnizel burger\n\nEven the beer bottles here are interesting — they have special flip-top caps. 🍺  The content on the beer bottle, money can not buy happiness, so drink.\n\nbeer\n\nLater, I dropped by Rewe and Rossmann to grab some supplements, cola beer, and the famous German-colored Fanta. 🇩🇪🥤, Surprisingly, the payment supports Alipay and wechat pay.\n\n\n\nRaw meat sandwich.\n\nMettstulle\n\nSushi in the store\n\nSushi\n\nHuge beer area\n\nbeer\n\nDifferent flavor Colas\n\ncola\n\nBrandenburg might not be the most tourist-friendly place, but its quiet charm, lakeside views, and authentic atmosphere make it a memorable stop on my journey through Germany. 🌿🇩🇪",
